   conditionally swapped based on hero-logo-collapsed or anything else —
   specifically so there is no discrete structural jump left anywhere:
   row 1 ("logo") always just auto-sizes to whatever .header__logo-hero's
   real height currently is, which is already a smooth, continuous,
   every-frame value from the SAME heroLogoScale() mechanism desktop
   uses (see the base rule above) — so the row visibly shrinking as the
   logo does is just that existing continuous animation, not a second
   one. Row 2 (icons) is a genuinely separate grid row, so it never
   competes with row 1 for height and needs no stabilization against
   drifting (unlike the single-shared-row layout, where the icons would
   recenter within a row growing/shrinking around them — confirmed via
   the equivalent, already-fixed desktop bug earlier this session,
