   opposed to a raw vw value) is what lets that narrowing propagate
   correctly through every column instead of overshooting by the
   scrollbar's width. The 1/4 width lives on .drawer-menu__bottom itself
   (not .drawer-menu__primary-links) — see the rule below — so every
   descendant in between just inherits 100% of an already-narrow ancestor;
   .drawer-menu__primary-links needs no width rule of its own in the
   default state, it falls back to the pre-existing
   `.drawer-menu__all-links ul{ width:100% }`. */
