/* Editorial slide-in, desktop only: the base (mobile) rule above this
   media query animates the panel with a plain opacity fade — fine for a
   full-width mobile takeover, but not the "enters from off-screen left"
   feel wanted here. Overriding transition here (not just adding a new
   transform rule) replaces that fade's duration/easing outright rather
   than layering a second one on top of it. Reuses the exact same
   .drawer-menu.active/.visible toggle the base rule already reacts to —
   no new JS state, so switching between categories (which never touches
   these two classes, only .drawer-menu__list--sub's own) can't retrigger
   it, and close() already runs this in reverse for free the moment
   .visible is removed. translateX is relative to the panel's OWN width,
   so this is correct unchanged at both the 80vw and 100vw sub-breakpoints
   below. See assets/theme.js's close() for the matching setTimeout delay
   this duration must stay under (bumped alongside this change) so the
   panel isn't hard-unmounted mid-slide. Was 550ms/300ms; slowed down on
   request — closeCleanupDelay in theme.js raised to match. Opacity now
   matches the transform's own 750ms exactly (was a shorter 300/400ms) —
   with opacity finishing well before the slide did, the panel visually
   vanished early and kept sliding invisibly for the rest of the
   duration, reported as hiding "too fast" despite the slide itself
   already being slower. */
