/* .drawer-menu__panel's z-index was raised above the header's own dark
   ::before bar (see the panel rule above) specifically so the menu's own
   white/image content wins over that bar everywhere, not just behind
   column 3's image — explicit request: the header should sit BEHIND the
   menu's white background, not superimposed over it. Plain solid
   background here (base rule, no override needed) is what lets that
   white simply reach y:0 uncontested, same as column 3's image already
   does — the ::before bar only ever shows through in the untouched
   franja beyond the 80vw panel, where nothing from the menu is painting
   over it at all. */
/* Columns 1/2's TEXT still needs to start below the header row (not
   under the X/search/logo/cart icons) even though the white background
   itself now runs the full height — this padding is what keeps JOYAS/
   COLECCIONES's own text clear of those icons; column 3's image
   deliberately cancels this same padding via its own negative top
   offset further down, since an image (unlike text) reading right up to
